      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**The work order is MO-25-09-1070 (ID: WO-2025-09-004), but I could not determine whether a late-created event exists because access to the supporting event records was denied.** The review is therefore incomplete—not a finding that no late event occurred.\n\n### Verified findings\n\n| Item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Operation | Modine, Racine–DeKoven |\n| Work order | **MO-25-09-1070 / WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Product | Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 / PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Recorded period status | `PENDING_CLOSE` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n\nThe timestamp is reproduced exactly as recorded; the source supplies no timezone or UTC offset.\n\n### Event details not verifiable\n\nThe accessible records contain work-order and cost-period data, but no cost-event rows. Reading the supporting records returned **403 — source role not granted**. Consequently, I cannot reliably identify the **source transaction, amount, event-created time, elapsed minutes after Pending Close, or recorded accounting status**, or conclude whether that status is consistent with policy. I requested an authorized event extract through the supervisor channel.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied *Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B* documentation, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225**, states that:\n\n- New transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting until the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nAn event-level conclusion therefore requires both its creation timestamp and its transaction type, as well as its recorded accounting status.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_70a840764a1f/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
